<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>source-map-brief.md</title><style>body{font:18px system-ui;line-height:1.6;max-width:1000px;margin:2rem auto;padding:1rem;color:#17252d;background:white}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}table{border-collapse:collapse}td,th{border:1px solid #777;padding:.5rem}a{color:#064b8c}</style><main><h1>Locate answers before drafting a research brief — learner brief</h1>
<p>Fictional Northstar Services training material.</p>
<h2>Questions</h2>
<p>Where are business description, management discussion, and audited statements located?
SEC historical guide: <a href="https://www.sec.gov/answers/reada10k.htm">https://www.sec.gov/answers/reada10k.htm</a>
Modified 2011-07-01. Open and record access date. This is orientation, not current filing law.</p>
<h2>Task</h2>
<p>Northstar&#39;s new analyst needs a map of where annual-report information lives before a training session. Produce a source-location brief, without interpreting any company&#39;s results.</p>
<h2>Actions</h2>
<ol>
<li>Read the request and restate its three questions in your own words.</li>
<li>Ask AI for a search plan and a table with one row per question; treat returned links as unverified.</li>
<li>Open the SEC guide and locate the relevant sections yourself; record the modification date.</li>
<li>Give the located passages or brief paraphrases to AI and ask it to populate the table without adding current requirements.</li>
<li>Check all three citations against the original, remove unsupported claims, and add one follow-up requiring current evidence.</li>
</ol>
<h2>Output</h2>
<p>Question; source title/URL; publisher; publication/access date; section; paraphrased answer; current-rule limitation; unresolved question.</p>
